Release	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-08-11T06:59:47.2946283Z [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/pulls/296","id":4249100289,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQYTy3M79RCAB","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/296","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/296.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/296.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/296","number":296,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: expose model routing as a machine-readable model_resolved event","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nModel routing was only observable as an English log record:\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"log\", \"level\": \"info\", \"message\": \"using explicit provider/model\", \"providerID\": \"formalai\", \"modelID\": \"formal-ai\" }\n```\n\nA supervisor that must *verify* routing — e.g. kill the run when the agent resolves anything other than the requested model — has to match prose. An ordinary reword upstream then silently disables a downstream safety check, and the log record is not emitted at all on some paths.\n\nFixes #295 (follow-up to #293 / #294, released as `js-0.25.8`).\n\n## Solution\n\nA new first-class event in the `OutputType` vocabulary, emitted **exactly once per run** on **every** resolution path — explicit `provider/model`, bare model id, and default:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"model_resolved\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-08-11T00:12:31.320Z\",\n  \"requested\": \"formalai/formal-ai\",\n  \"selector\": \"formalai/formal-ai\",\n  \"providerID\": \"formalai\",\n  \"modelID\": \"formal-ai\",\n  \"source\": \"cli\",\n  \"matchesRequest\": true\n}\n```\n\n- `requested` — raw `--model`/`-m` value, `null` when nothing was requested.\n- `selector` — what was actually applied (`requested`, or the effective default), so `matchesRequest` is explicable when `requested` is `null`.\n- `source` — `cli` (from `--model`/`-m`), `config` (operator default via `LINK_ASSISTANT_AGENT_DEFAULT_MODEL` / `defaultOptions.defaultModel`), `default` (built-in `DEFAULT_MODEL`).\n- `matchesRequest` — whether `providerID`/`modelID` satisfies `selector`. A qualified selector must match both parts; a bare selector names only the model. Today the only in-tree path that makes this `false` is `--use-existing-claude-oauth` substituting `claude-oauth/claude-sonnet-4-5`.\n\n**Where it is emitted:** at the end of `parseModelConfig()`, which is the earliest point where the effective model is final — after resolution *and* after `--use-existing-claude-oauth`, the one override that can still replace an already selected model, and before session creation and any completion request. So the attestation can never lie, and a consumer can terminate the run before a request reaches a provider it did not ask for.\n\n**Claude standard:** `convertOpenCodeToClaude` now populates the already-declared optional `model` on the `init` event with `providerID/modelID`. Under `--json-standard claude` / `--output-format stream-json` the attestation is forced compact so the NDJSON stream stays one JSON object per line.\n\nThe existing `Log.Default.info({ message: 'using explicit provider/model', ... })` record is **unchanged** — this change is purely additive (`git diff js/src/cli/model-config.js` shows insertions only).\n\n## How to reproduce / verify manually\n\n```bash\ncd js\nbun experiments/model-resolved-fake-provider.mjs                  # opencode standard\nFMT=stream-json bun experiments/model-resolved-fake-provider.mjs  # claude standard\nMODEL= bun experiments/model-resolved-fake-provider.mjs           # default path\n```\n\nThe probe runs the real CLI against a local fake OpenAI-compatible provider and prints the event order plus the time of the first upstream request:\n\n```\nevent order: [\"config\",\"status\",\"input\",\"model_resolved\",...,\"step_start\",\"text\",\"step_finish\",...]\nmodel_resolved: {\"type\":\"model_resolved\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"requested\":\"formalai/formal-ai\",\"selector\":\"formalai/formal-ai\",\"providerID\":\"formalai\",\"modelID\":\"formal-ai\",\"source\":\"cli\",\"matchesRequest\":true}\ninit (stream-json): {\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"session_id\":\"ses_...\",\"model\":\"formalai/formal-ai\"}\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n`js/tests/model-resolved-event.ts` (unit, runs in CI):\n\n- asserts the literal `type` string `'model_resolved'`, so a reword of the human-readable log cannot silently change the machine contract;\n- payload shape, `requested: null` on the default path, and `matchesRequest: false` for the oauth-style substitution;\n- `selectorMatchesModel` for qualified / bare / `@scope/model` selectors;\n- child-process runs of the real `parseModelConfig`: `--model formalai/formal-ai` → one event, `source: \"cli\"`; `--model formal-ai` → one event, `source: \"cli\"`; no `--model` → one event, `source: \"default\"`, `requested: null`; `LINK_ASSISTANT_AGENT_DEFAULT_MODEL` set → `source: \"config\"`;\n- `--json-standard claude` keeps the event on a single NDJSON line;\n- an unknown explicit model still fails closed (non-zero exit, no attestation) — #293 behaviour preserved.\n\n`js/tests/json-standard-unit.js` (unit, runs in CI): `init` omits `model` when none is supplied and reports it when it is; the claude event handler carries it through.\n\n`js/tests/integration/model-resolved-event.js` (fake local provider, no network): exactly one event per run; emitted before the first `step_start`; its timestamp is `<=` the fake provider's first request time; under `--output-format stream-json` a single NDJSON line and `init.model === \"formalai/formal-ai\"`.\n\n`js/tests/integration/json-standard-claude.js`: `model_resolved` added to the valid claude event types.\n\nLocal run: `bun run test` → 717 pass / 0 fail; `npm run check` (eslint + prettier + file-size) clean.\n\n## Docs\n\n- `docs/model-resolved-event.md` — field table, ordering guarantees, why not to parse the log message, shell example.\n- `examples/verify-model-routing.mjs` — supervisor that kills the run when `matchesRequest` is `false`.\n- README pointers (root + `js/`).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Changeset `js/.changeset/model-resolved-event.md` (minor — additive feature) triggers the next release.\n- Unrelated observation, not changed here: with `--use-existing-claude-oauth`, compaction `\"same\"` still binds to the *pre*-substitution model, because compaction parsing runs before the oauth override. Worth a separate issue.\n- `js/tests/integration/json-standard-claude.js` has pre-existing staleness (its `validTypes` / `initIndex === 0` assertions do not account for the `config`/`status`/`input` envelope events the CLI emits); this PR only adds `model_resolved` to that list and does not attempt to fix the rest.\n","created_at":"2026-08-10T23:54:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T06:56:18Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T06:56:18Z","merged_at":"2026-08-11T06:56:18Z","merge_commit_sha":"af533da87e7617fe6450504c70687c1937491104","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconten